      "summary": "Langfuse is retiring automatic token estimates and highlighting missing usage so teams can identify instrumentation gaps behind absent costs.",
      "body": [
        "Langfuse is an AI observability platform that records model generations and calculates their costs. Its new changelog explains why it is retiring automatic tokenization: estimating token counts from a generation’s input and output when an integration sends no usage. According to Langfuse, reasoning models and cached-token pricing can make those estimates incorrect while hiding broken instrumentation.",
        "First, generation headers now identify missing token usage and link to guidance for fixing the integration. This helps distinguish a missing usage record from a missing model price when a generation has no cost. Teams that relied on automatic estimates should then update their instrumentation to send usage reported by the model provider, or submit costs directly. Langfuse continues calculating costs from submitted usage and model prices; integrations already sending usage or costs need no change.",
